  "statement": "Write a function named `calculate_average(numbers)` that takes a non-empty list of numbers and returns their arithmetic mean (average) as a floating-point number.\n\nThe arithmetic mean is the sum of all elements divided by the total count of elements:\n$$\\text{Average} = \\frac{\\sum \\text{numbers}}{N}$$\n\n### Examples\n- `calculate_average([10, 20, 30])` returns `20.0`\n- `calculate_average([1, 2, 3, 4])` returns `2.5`\n- `calculate_average([5])` returns `5.0`",
